<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arcetri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arcetri is a hilly district on the southern edge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo Galilei</a> moved there in 1631, to his villa Il Gioiello near the convent where his daughter was a nun, and after his condemnation by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> in 1633 he lived there under house arrest until his death in 1642. The Arcetri Astrophysical Observatory, founded in the nineteenth century, continues the area's scientific association.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arcetri.jpg" alt="Arcetri" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sailko · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torre_del_gallo.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
